+# PnP private authenticated remote Lean build transport — design note
+
+Status: **design-only; implementation blocked by missing authorized private channel**.
+Owner context: Executive engineering transport task (Founder handoff H-1795547911-c50a),
+study `records/research/2026-11-24-founder-proof-production-study.md` section 5.
+Date: 2026-11-24 UTC.
+
+## Problem
+
+marceline-dev (32 cores / 62 GiB RAM) can compile Lean proofs faster than billy-dev
+(4 cores / 15 GiB RAM), but the two hosts do not resolve each other and no SSH
+listener was observed. Both hosts have authenticated GitHub SSH outbound and the
+Viche repository is public. Unpublished proof sources and credentials must never be
+placed in public refs or public artifacts. No new spending and no new network
+listener are authorized.
+
+## Hard constraints
+
+- Pin base revision and Lean/toolchain; validate exact source/statement before build.
+- Isolate a scratch worktree; deduplicate exact source digests.
+- Cap memory/time to checker limits; cancel obsolete jobs; cache diagnostics.
+- Parallelize under measured headroom; persistent cached build workers.
+- Do not add a second MANDATORY redundant build.
+- No public proof relay; no access-control bypass; no unpublished proof sources or
+  credentials in public refs/artifacts; no new spending; no new network listener.
+
+## Proposed design (minimal)
+
+### 1. Source package (billy-dev, sender)
+
+- Input: exact `base_revision` (Viche/PnP repo commit), `toolchain` (elan/lean
+  toolchain identifier and hash), target gap/lemma identifier, and a minimal source
+  manifest listing only files required for the proof check.
+- Compute `source_digest = sha256(canonical_manifest + sorted(file_digest, path))`.
+  Canonical manifest is UTF-8, LF, sorted paths, no timestamps.
+- Validate before packaging: exact target statement/module/path/imports match the
+  held gap/desk metadata; reject if statement drifted; record validation result.
+- Create an isolated scratch git worktree at `base_revision`; overlay only the
+  manifest files; verify overlay paths are inside the scratch root.
+- Package as a deterministic tar (sorted, fixed mtime/uid/gid, no xattrs) then
+  encrypt+authenticate before leaving the host. Plaintext unpublished sources never
+  written to a public location.
+
+### 2. Private authenticated transport
+
+The transport carries only encrypted, authenticated blobs addressed by
+`source_digest`. It must provide confidentiality, integrity, sender/receiver
+authentication, and access control limited to billy-dev and marceline-dev operators.
+
+**Required external authorization/channel (not currently available):**
+
+- **Option A (preferred, uses existing GitHub SSH outbound):** a Founder-authorized
+  **private GitHub repository** (or private GitHub Package/container/blob store with
+  SSH/Git auth) dedicated to encrypted build bundles. Both hosts already have
+  authenticated GitHub SSH outbound; authorization needed is: create the private
+  repo, grant the existing billy-dev and marceline-dev GitHub identities read/write
+  access, and approve its use for encrypted unpublished-proof build bundles. No new
+  listener, no new spending if within existing GitHub plan; public Viche repo remains
+  clean. Bundle objects are encrypted before push; only ciphertext and digests appear
+  in the private repo.
+- **Option B:** an authorized private object store or SSH endpoint reachable by both
+  hosts over existing authorized outbound paths, with credentials provisioned through
+  an existing secret channel. This needs explicit Founder authorization of endpoint,
+  credentials, and spending/network policy.
+- **Option C:** Founder-authorized Tailscale/WireGuard/private tunnel. Rejected under
+  current constraints unless separately authorized: it changes network exposure and
+  may require new listeners/services/spending decisions.
+
+No option is implemented because no existing private authenticated channel for
+unpublished proof sources was observed (see Evidence).
+
+### 3. Remote build worker (marceline-dev)
+
+- Persistent worker polls the authorized private channel for new digest jobs; no
+  inbound listener.
+- Deduplicate by `source_digest`: if cached result exists for same
+  `(base_revision, toolchain, source_digest, checker_limits)`, return cached
+  diagnostics/artifact metadata.
+- For new jobs: fetch ciphertext, verify authentication, decrypt locally in a tmpfs
+  or private work dir, materialize scratch worktree at pinned `base_revision`, apply
+  overlay, verify manifest digests, verify exact target statement.
+- Run Lean/check under cgroups/resource limits: memory cap <= checker limit and below
+  measured marceline-dev headroom; wall-clock timeout; cancel obsolete jobs when a
+  newer digest for same target supersedes them.
+- Capture deterministic diagnostics: exit code, elapsed time, peak RSS, toolchain
+  version, base revision, source digest, target statement hash, stdout/stderr logs.
+- Upload only authorized artifacts (diagnostics, pass/fail, possibly encrypted proof
+  artifact if separately authorized) back through the same private channel. Never
+  publish unpublished proof sources.
+
+### 4. Local coordinator (billy-dev)
+
+- Submits jobs, polls for results, maintains local cache keyed by digest.
+- Makes remote build optional/non-mandatory: local build remains possible; remote
+  build is an accelerator when authorized and healthy.
+- Parallelizes independent digests under measured headroom; does not overload
+  marceline-dev shared capacity.
+
+### 5. Security/integrity checks
+
+- Authenticate ciphertext (AEAD, e.g. age/libsodium/XChaCha20-Poly1305) with keys
+  distributed out-of-band through Founder-authorized secret management.
+- Include `base_revision`, `toolchain`, `source_digest`, `statement_hash`,
+  `created_at`, `sender` in signed manifest.
+- Reject unknown schema versions, digest mismatches, statement mismatches, or
+  toolchain mismatches.
+- Never log plaintext source or keys; diagnostics are scrubbed before upload.
+
+## Evidence (local, non-invasive)
+
+- Study section 5: "Neither resolves the other hostname; separate network namespaces,
+  no SSH listener observed. Both have authenticated GitHub SSH outbound, Viche
+  repository is PUBLIC. Do not put unpublished proof sources or credentials in public
+  relay refs."
+- `git remote -v`: `origin git@github.com:ottojung/viche.git` (public repo).
+- `gh auth status`: not logged into any GitHub host.
+- `~/.ssh/config`: absent; `ssh -G marceline-dev` shows default unresolved hostname
+  `marceline-dev` (no configured private transport).
+- No `marceline` transport configuration found in `/var/lib/lubko/wd/viche-state/pnp`.
+- No probe/scan/connection attempt was made to marceline-dev or any undeclared host.
+
+## Exact authorization needed
+
+Founder authorization to create/use a **private authenticated channel** for encrypted
+build bundles, preferably a private GitHub repository accessible via existing
+GitHub SSH identities on billy-dev and marceline-dev, with explicit approval that
+encrypted unpublished proof sources may transit that private repo. The authorization
+should name: repo/location, allowed identities, retention/deletion policy, who may
+decrypt, and confirmation that no public refs/artifacts will carry plaintext or keys.
